Here's a simple HTML website that displays a random joke from a list of 4 jokes when a user clicks a button.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Joke Generator</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>Joke Generator</h1>
        <button onclick="getRandomJoke()">Get Joke</button>
        <div id="joke"></div>
    </div>

    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

<style>
    .container {
        width: 300px;
        margin: auto;
        padding: 20px;
        background-color: #f0f0f0;
    }

    button {
        padding: 10px 20px;
        font-size: 16px;
        cursor: pointer;
    }

    #joke {
        font-size: 18px;
        color: #333;
    }
</style>

<script src="script.js"></script>
```

**script.js:**
```javascript
const jokes = [
    "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!",
    "What do you call a fake noodle? An impasta!",
    "Why did the scarecrow win an award? Because he was outstanding in his field!",
    "Why did the chicken get a drivers license? Because it wanted to apply for a poultry permit!"
];

function getRandomJoke() {
    const jokeIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length);
    document.getElementById("joke").textContent = jokes[jokeIndex];
}
```

This website uses JavaScript to generate a random joke from the list when the button is clicked. The `getRandomJoke` function selects a random index from the `jokes` array and updates the `#joke` element with the selected joke.
